p/x TMPDIR=/private/tmp/y PATH=\\\"$PATH\\\" npx vitest run; then same env with npx vitest run --maxWorkers=1 --no-file-parallelism; node tests/fixtures/process-bounds/inventory.mjs out.json; baseline repro: git show ba292a0:src/cli/agent-version.ts > $R/install/src/cli/agent-version.ts with evaluator git shim (EV_GIT_MODE=stall) first on PATH, run under probes/ev-watchdog.mjs 5000 and observe watchdog SIGKILL at ~5013ms.\"\n30\t    },\n31\t    {\n32\t      \"feature_id\": \"F005\",\n33\t      \"result\": \"PASS\",\n34\t      \"evidence\": \"This fresh Kimi-family evaluation performed F005 itself: verified repo.ref SHA 3130cef3bc55528290c49ee35267e1aff33b5c78 matches HEAD; read spec/evaluator.md/progress from disk; treated Generator/historical reports as claims; independently derived and ran real-subprocess adversarial controls for SIGTERM resistance, descendants retaining pipes, output overflow, failed supervision (mid-flight worker death), startup SHA snapshot, and preview/valid-confirmation replay refusal with byte-identical queue/cursor/config; verified owned child cleanup and target-ENOENT vs supervisor-failure distinction; inspected shared replay deadline, output bounds and privacy/queue regressions; reran lint/verify/build/focused/full-default/full-controlled with results above; saved detailed report, raw logs and new probe tests under docs/test-reports/BL-REPLAY-PROCESS-BOUNDS-kimi-20261008/. Local macOS acceptance limits truthfully recorded (no native Windows/Linux, no PG16, no browser/original F005, no production gates, no hard-real-time claim for blocked syscalls/suspended OS/escaped groups). No push, no commit, no gate decision written, no real-home/personal access, no product/spec/old-evidence modification.\",\n35\t      \"steps_to_reproduce\": \"Read docs/test-reports/BL-REPLAY-PROCESS-BOUNDS-kimi-20261008/README.md and the raw logs/probes in that directory; verdict schema .claude/autonomous/verdict-artifact.schema.json; signoff at docs/test-reports/BL