{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_HwIH8ypxBo99lX8vIrncgUnX","content":"1\t# AGENTS.md\n2\t\n3\t本仓库的**唯一真源是 [CLAUDE.md](./CLAUDE.md)** —— 角色、状态机、命令、硬约束都在那里，\n4\t本文件只做外部 CLI（Codex / Kimi 等）入口的指路牌，不重复内容以免两份漂移。\n5\t\n6\t## 开工前必读\n7\t\n8\t1. `harness-rules.md` —— 状态机、角色、独立性铁则、机制化守门\n9\t2. `CLAUDE.md` —— 本项目的技术栈、命令、硬约束（尤其「push main = 部署生产」）\n10\t3. 当前状态：`progress.json.status` 决定你该进哪个角色入口\n11\t\n12\t## 对外部 agent 的额外约束\n13\t\n14\t- **你不得推送任何分支**，产物留在自己的 worktree 里，由编排者回流（`framework/harness/dispatch-mode.md` §6）\n15\t- **你不得写 `pending_gate.decision`** —— 人闸门归人，机器侧 hook 会当场拒\n16\t- 结论必须落成产物文件（verdict.json / diff），不靠对话传递（铁律 12）"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_rqNOXecwX2Agufeuk167Ncv2","content":"1\t# Scoped local signoff — BL-REPLAY-PROCESS-BOUNDS (NOT production ready)\n2\t\n3\tScope: local macOS acceptance of F001–F004 plus F005 independent acceptance at\n4\t`3130cef3bc55528290c49ee35267e1aff33b5c78` only.\n5\t\n6\tThe independent Kimi-family evaluation is complete: all refusal/bounding controls were\n7\tre-derived from the spec and actual code (never from Generator claims), executed as real\n8\tsubprocesses under synthetic homes with external watchdogs and owned-only cleanup, and all\n9\tstandard gates were rerun green in a fresh-install sandbox. Full method, evidence, retained\n10\tfailure logs and limitations: `BL-REPLAY-PROCESS-BOUNDS-kimi-20261008/README.md`; machine\n11\tverdict: `BL-REPLAY-PROCESS-BOUNDS-verdict.json`.\n12\t\n13\tThis signoff is explicitly bounded:\n14\t\n15\t- **Release readiness: false.** Native Windows/Linux execution, exact-SHA CI, real PG16,\n16\t  authenticated browser / original homepage F005, service installers, production/staging and\n17\t  the full B03/B07 programme were not executed and are not inferred from local macOS results.\n18\t  Windows-only tests are recorded as explicit macOS skips, not passes.\n19\t- Timing results are scheduling allowances (startup 2,000 ms + declared 2,000 ms allowance;\n20\t  replay 10,000 ms operation deadline with reserved cleanup), not hard real-time guarantees:\n21\t  blocked synchronous filesystem syscalls, OS-suspended workers, deliberately escaped process\n22\t  groups and an unresponsive OS remain outside the enforced bound, matching the product's own\n23\t  declaration.\n24\t- The heavyweight baseline replay end-to-end reproduction (Generator's\n25\t  `baseline-reproduction.log`) was not rerun by this evaluator (time-boxed); baseline F1 was\n26\t  independently reproduced on exact `ba292a0` bytes, and baseline F2 was confirmed by code\n27\t  inspection plus empirically proven SIGTERM resistance of the evaluator's own shim.\n28\t- npm audit findings (Generator-recorded: 7 high) remain unremediated by design; this evaluator\n29\t  used `--no-audit` and did not re-derive them. No dependency changes occurred in this batch.\n30\t- Test-authoring note for future work only (not a defect): `git.ts` caches GitInfo per\n31\t  workspace per process; replay refusal controls must run each invocation in a fresh process.\n32\t- No human gate decision was written; `progress.json`/`features.json` transitions are left to\n33\t  the Coordinator. Nothing was pushed, deployed or committed by this evaluator.\n34\t\n35\tSigned: Kimi evaluator instance `replay-process-bounds-3130cef-kimi-r0`, 2026-10-08 (UTC 2026-10-08T04:01Z)."}
